## Pin provenance

A copied tree carries no git history, so its upstream commit was not recorded. Where the tree states a version and upstream has a tag for exactly that version, the tag's commit is a real pin and the version string is the evidence. Each row below was read from the file named, not inferred.

| id | version in the tree | upstream tag | pinned to | evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `brotli` | 1.2.0 | `v1.2.0` | `028fb5a23661` | `old/brotli-master/c/common/version.h` |
| `libbsc` | 3.4.0 | `v3.4.0` | `4d823bc57ca1` | `old/libbsc-master/VERSION` |
| `libdeflate` | 1.26 | `v1.26` | `92e6a0db9fa8` | `old/libdeflate-master/libdeflate.h` |
| `xz` | 5.8.4 | `v5.8.4` | `d3e650e63c11` | `old/xz-master/src/liblzma/api/lzma/version.h` |
| `zpaq` | 7.15 | `7.15` | `9ab539f644e3` | `old/zpaq-master/zpaq.cpp` |

These stay `copy`, with the reason: `zstd` states 1.6.0 and `lz4` states 1.10.1, and neither has a tag of that name — the copied trees are ahead of the last release, and a pin to the previous tag would be a claim the tree contradicts. `advancecomp`'s `configure.ac` reads `AC_INIT([AdvanceCOMP], [git_revision], ...)`, which is a placeholder, not a version. `zopfli`, `packJPG`, `precomp-cpp`, `bitshuffle`, `parmar`, `zlib-ng`, `freearc-c`, `freearc-main`, `FA-master`, `srep`, `LPAQ9`, `BARF`, `BBB`, `FLZP`, `FPAQF2` and `SR3A` state no version in a file this vault can read.

## Submodule entries

23 rows above are `git submodule` entries, pinned by the commit SHA recorded in
the tree and mapped to their upstream URL in `.gitmodules`. Materialise them with
`git submodule update --init --recursive`, and verify with
`./scripts/check-vendor.sh`.

`pin` is `TBD` in the table because the authoritative pin is the gitlink SHA in
the tree, not a value maintained by hand here. To read a pin:

```bash
git ls-tree HEAD old/ | awk '$1=="160000"{print $4, $3}'
```

